{"source_id": "nasa-99b341840ed423878c622478b3b7817729d0ccf4d772f407f860a91d66972917", "content_sha256": "99b341840ed423878c622478b3b7817729d0ccf4d772f407f860a91d66972917", "experiment": "PSI-117", "filename": "PSI-117_Presentations_Three_Stage_Cool_Flame_TFarouk.pdf", "file_type": "pdf", "source_path": "psi-117/PSI-117_Presentations_Three_Stage_Cool_Flame_TFarouk.pdf", "document_type": "unknown", "evidence_status": null, "text": "16\nExperimental Observation of 3 Stage Behavior\nFLEX 1268:\nn-dodecane, 2.75 atm, 21.6% O2, 50.2% N2,\n28.2% He.\nQualitative agreement between\npredictions and observations\nAtef et al. Combustion and Flame (2017)", "source_locator": "page:16", "page_number": 16, "document_metadata": {"title": "Slide 1", "author": "Tanvir Farouk", "created": "D:20260428082902-04'00'", "modified": "D:20260428082908-04'00'", "producer": "Adobe PDF Library 26.1.183"}, "extraction_warnings": [], "source_url": "https://psi.nasa.gov/physci/repo/data/investigations/PSI-117", "source_accession": "PSI-117", "chunk_id": "chunk-3b83bd04facbd2df4ad6ad18ad68441ae5da4182e951e1dbf9490078d7e1c0e2", "chunk_index": 1, "chunk_count": 1, "estimated_token_count": 72}
{"source_id": "nasa-99b341840ed423878c622478b3b7817729d0ccf4d772f407f860a91d66972917", "content_sha256": "99b341840ed423878c622478b3b7817729d0ccf4d772f407f860a91d66972917", "experiment": "PSI-117", "filename": "PSI-117_Presentations_Three_Stage_Cool_Flame_TFarouk.pdf", "file_type": "pdf", "source_path": "psi-117/PSI-117_Presentations_Three_Stage_Cool_Flame_TFarouk.pdf", "document_type": "unknown", "evidence_status": null, "text": "17\nSummary\n• The experimental results and detailed predictions support that\nthere exists two possible modes of quasi-steady cool flame\ndroplet burning behaviour: “Warm” in the NTC regime and “Cold”\nin the low temperature regime.\n• The helium concentration is critical for the observed\ncharacteristics – promoting the second stage burn or completely\nsupressing it.\n• A dynamic coupling between heat generation and heat loss in\nthe system.\n• The low temperature kinetics is distinctive and different in the\nsecond and third stage.\n• Experimental observation with n-dodecane at higher pressure\nand helium exchange validates the “a priori” numerical\npredictions of a three stage behaviour inferred from n-heptane\nsimulations.", "source_locator": "page:17", "page_number": 17, "document_metadata": {"title": "Slide 1", "author": "Tanvir Farouk", "created": "D:20260428082902-04'00'", "modified": "D:20260428082908-04'00'", "producer": "Adobe PDF Library 26.1.183"}, "extraction_warnings": [], "source_url": "https://psi.nasa.gov/physci/repo/data/investigations/PSI-117", "source_accession": "PSI-117", "chunk_id": "chunk-12ca3b68c3b09abd5fdf10ddb155b28dc10d7642660c8dd4ec04d38b94d56ec9", "chunk_index": 1, "chunk_count": 1, "estimated_token_count": 207}
